        <mxCell id="c255" value="&lt;i&gt;Outlined in teal: the six named parameter cells, each with its name in the tag beside it (the Name Box shows B15&#x27;s, whose formula reads the size from the table by two lookups). In coral: the cells the plan reads, a size of 59 at 95% confidence, a 5% tolerable rate and no expected deviation, 0 deviations allowed, and the only row of the rule that supports reliance. In blue: why each of the 7 key items is key (6 are customer 128&#x27;s, whose refunds total 26,315.10) and the rows of the rule whose limit is above the tolerable rate. Long labels are cut and columns narrower than the workbook&#x27;s.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="892" width="860" height="68" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
